WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.620
Trace the cooling path from the equipment through its connections and manifold

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:04.460
to the receiving loop.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.640
A coolant distribution unit may separate a technology cooling system from a

4
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:09.800
facility water system.

5
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.180
Those boundaries can have different fluid chemistry, pressure and temperature conditions.

6
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.820
The animation reveals each handoff without implying that every installation has the

7
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:19.640
same topology.

8
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.360
At each connection, identify which side provides the required conditions and how

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.080
they are verified.

10
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.800
Matching a coupling size isn't enough: materials, fluid specification, pressure limits and

11
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.120
the operating temperature range must also agree.

12
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.080
Flow requirements apply at defined conditions.

13
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.320
The receiving system must provide the required hydraulic performance for the configured

14
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.020
circuit, while heat rejection must support the permitted operating envelope.

15
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.500
Avoid swapping a pump rating for evidence at the equipment boundary.

16
00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.440
We'll study the cooling interfaces and service evidence in more depth in

17
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.140
module seven.

18
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.040
For now, the essential result is a complete loop map with no

19
00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.800
hidden assumption about where the heat, pressure or fluid-compatibility responsibility goes.

